        "name": "USN-7808-1",
        "description": "Several security issues were discovered in the Linux kernel. An attacker could possibly use these to compromise the system. This update corrects flaws in the following subsystems:   - Network drivers;   - Ext4 file system;   - SMB network file system;   - Packet sockets;   - Network traffic control;   - TLS protocol;   - VMware vSockets driver;   - XFRM subsystem; (CVE-2025-38617, CVE-2025-37785, CVE-2025-38244, CVE-2025-37756, CVE-2025-38618, CVE-2025-38477, CVE-2025-38683, CVE-2025-38500)",
